# LINE ENDINGS ARE A DEPLOYMENT CONCERN HERE, NOT A STYLE ONE.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) and runs inside
# Linux containers. That combination works only for as long as every clone
# happens to have the same local git config, which is not a property a buyer's
# IT department can be expected to know about.
#
# Without this file the guarantee is per-machine. With it, it is per-repository:
# the index stays LF and the checkout is normalised regardless of who cloned it
# or how their git is configured.
#
# The concrete failure this prevents: a shell script committed with CRLF gets
# copied into an image and the kernel reads the shebang as "/bin/sh\r", which
# fails with the famously unhelpful
#
#     exec /app/entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory
#
# backend/entrypoint.sh is the container's entrypoint, so that is a container
# that will not boot at all — on the buyer's hardware, not ours.

# Normalise everything git detects as text to LF in the index.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that MUST be LF because something other than an editor reads them.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.bash      text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf
entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf
Caddyfile*  text eol=lf

# Source and config: LF, explicitly, so the intent survives a future edit to
# the glob above.
*.py        text eol=lf
*.js        text eol=lf
*.jsx       text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.css       text eol=lf
*.html      text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.sql       text eol=lf
*.txt       text eol=lf
.env.example text eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these. A "text" conversion applied to an image or an
# archive corrupts it silently, and the corruption only shows up when someone
# opens the file rather than when it is committed.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.svg       text eol=lf
*.woff      binary
*.woff2     binary
*.ttf       binary
*.pdf       binary
*.zip       binary
*.gz        binary
*.tar       binary
*.dump      binary
*.snapshot  binary
